SUMMARY:Nate Bargatze: Big Dumb Eyes World Tour LIVE at SAP Center at San Jose
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nNate Bargatze is one of the biggest names in stand-up comedy today — a clean\, family-friendly comedian from Nashville\, Tennessee\, whose laid-back Southern charm and masterful storytelling have made him a household name. Known as “The Great Nate\,” Bargatze has sold out arenas across the country and earned a reputation as one of the most beloved live performers in the business. \nHis comedy is warm\, relatable\, and brilliantly crafted — drawing from his life as a husband\, father\, and son of a clown (yes\, really). Nate’s specials on Netflix\, including The Greatest Average American and Hello World\, have introduced him to millions of fans worldwide and cemented his status as a comedy superstar. \nThe Big Dumb Eyes World Tour is Bargatze’s most ambitious tour yet\, bringing his signature brand of wholesome\, hilarious comedy to arenas across the globe. This is a rare chance to see one of comedy’s biggest stars in the Bay Area — don’t miss it. \nEvent Details\nDate: Friday\, July 17\, 2026\nTime: 7:00 PM PDT\nVenue: SAP Center at San Jose\, 525 W Santa Clara St\, San Jose\, CA 95113\nTicket Price Range: $65 – $150 \nAbout the Venue\nSAP Center at San Jose is one of the premier entertainment arenas in the Bay Area\, located at 525 W Santa Clara Street in downtown San Jose. With a capacity of approximately 17\,500 for concerts and events\, SAP Center is home to the San Jose Sharks NHL team and hosts some of the biggest touring acts in the world. \nThe arena features state-of-the-art sound and lighting systems\, multiple concession areas\, full bar service\, and a variety of seating options from floor-level to upper bowl. Parking is available in several nearby garages and surface lots\, and the venue is conveniently located near the SAP Center Light Rail station for easy public transit access. \nSeeing Nate Bargatze at SAP Center means experiencing his comedy at full arena scale — a massive production with incredible energy from thousands of fans all laughing together. It’s a truly special experience. \nWhat to Expect\nThe Big Dumb Eyes World Tour is a full arena stand-up show featuring Nate Bargatze’s best new material alongside fan favorites. Expect a polished\, high-production performance with Bargatze’s signature storytelling style — slow-burn setups\, perfectly timed punchlines\, and the kind of wholesome humor that appeals to audiences of all ages. \nThis is an all-ages show\, making it a perfect night out for the whole family. Doors typically open 60–90 minutes before showtime. Arrive early to find your seats and grab concessions before the show begins. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $65 – $150 (before taxes and fees)\nTickets are available through Ticketmaster (official) and VividSeats (resale). \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/nate-bargatze-big-dumb-eyes-world-tour-live-at-sap-center-at-san-jose/
LOCATION:SAP Center at San Jose\, 525 W Santa Clara St\, San Jose\, California\, 95113\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://comedycalendar.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/969958b2-3e23-41ae-a1e8-8be73f5463af_CUSTOM-IMFUca.jpg
GEO:37.3328955;-121.9010841
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=SAP Center at San Jose 525 W Santa Clara St San Jose California 95113 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=525 W Santa Clara St:geo:-121.9010841,37.3328955
END:VEVENT
