SUMMARY:Ryan Long LIVE at The Wilbur
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Performer\nRyan Long is a comedian\, podcaster\, and filmmaker originally from Toronto who has amassed billions of views across his viral sketches\, street interviews\, and stand-up clips. Known for his sharp political satire\, his man-on-the-street videos\, and his ability to skewer both sides of the political aisle with equal wit\, Ryan has built one of the most loyal and diverse fanbases in comedy. \nHis live stand-up shows bring all of that energy to the stage in a full-length performance that fans have been waiting to see. Ryan’s comedy is smart\, fearless\, and brilliantly crafted — the kind of stand-up that makes you laugh and think at the same time. \nWith billions of online views and a rapidly growing live following\, Ryan Long at The Wilbur is one of the most exciting comedy shows coming to Boston this summer. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Friday\, July 17\, 2026\nTime: 7:30 PM ET\nVenue: The Wilbur\, 246 Tremont St\, Boston\, MA 02116\nTickets from: $63\n\nAbout the Venue\nThe Wilbur is one of Boston’s most beloved and intimate comedy venues\, located in the heart of the Theater District at 246 Tremont Street. With a capacity of approximately 1\,000 guests\, The Wilbur offers an up-close and personal experience that is perfect for Ryan’s sharp and engaging performance style. \nThe venue features excellent sightlines from every seat\, a full bar\, and a warm\, historic atmosphere that makes every show feel special. Originally built in 1914\, The Wilbur has been lovingly restored and is now one of the premier comedy destinations on the East Coast. \nParking is available at nearby garages in the Theater District\, and the venue is easily accessible via the MBTA Green and Orange Lines at Boylston and Back Bay stations. \nWhat to Expect\nExpect a sharp\, funny\, and brilliantly entertaining evening of stand-up comedy as Ryan Long takes the stage at The Wilbur. This is a solo performance showcasing Ryan’s signature blend of political satire\, observational humor\, and the kind of fearless comedy that has made him one of the most talked-about comedians online. \nSuitable for audiences 16 and older. A perfect summer night out for fans of smart\, sharp stand-up comedy. \nTicket Information\nTickets from $63. Purchase official tickets through Ticketmaster or find resale tickets via VividSeats. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/ryan-long-live-at-the-wilbur/
LOCATION:The Wilbur\, 246 Tremont St.\, Boston\, MA\, 2116
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://s1.ticketm.net/dam/a/e84/6987917a-5bcc-4f1c-b69f-06bbf9422e84_TABLET_LANDSCAPE_LARGE_16_9.jpg
